<title>UK: Sakura Bank unit sets $600 mln step-up FRN.</title>
<headline>Sakura Bank unit sets $600 mln step-up FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager Merrill Lynch.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SAKURA CAPITAL FUNDING (CAYMAN) LTD</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  SAKURA BANK LTD</p>
<p> AMT    $600 MLN	BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY  **PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN  ** +90 BP    PAY DATE    11.SEP.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY BAA2	ISS PRICE  PAR	 FULL FEES   0.75</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   BBB	 REOFFER    PAR</p>
<p> NOTES    **UNTIL 11.SEP.02 WHEN COUPON STEPS UP TO 3M LIBOR</p>
<p>		PLUS 240 BP IF NOT CALLED AT PAR</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP/CI</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.50	SELL CONC  0.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	SAKURA FINANCE INTERNATIONAL IS JOINT LEAD MANAGER</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
